# Week 1 — HTML5, CSS3 & Responsive Web Design

## Project: Orbit Log
A mission-control style dashboard for tracking rocket launches, featured missions, and a mission-watch sign-up log. This is the running project for the whole internship — it started as plain HTML this week and is meant to keep evolving through JS, React, TypeScript, and a real API later on.

| Day | Focus | Status |
|-----|-------|--------|
| Day 1 | HTML5 Foundations | Done |
| Day 2 | CSS Fundamentals | Done |
| Day 3 | Modern CSS Layout (Flexbox/Grid) | Done |
| Day 4 | Responsive Web Design | Done |
| Day 5 | Weekly Project & Revision | Not started |

## How each day builds on the last

- **Day 1** — just structure, no styling. Semantic HTML, a table, a form.
- **Day 2** — added `style.css`, gave it a mission-control look (dark background, orange/cyan accents, custom fonts).
- **Day 3** — rebuilt the nav as Flexbox, added a stats row using Flexbox cards, turned the mission list into a real CSS Grid.
- **Day 4** — made it actually responsive: breakpoints, a working mobile nav without JavaScript, scalable type, a scrollable table on small screens.
